		{
			"id":"466ae733cf49e983",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\"output\": \"Specialist brief — Daily Product Execution (one-page top-level summary + 3–5 prioritized attention items). Data sources: Kruise Flow daily reports (25–26 Aug), Kruise CRM (26 Aug), Inspecto (26 Aug), Stock Management (26 Aug), and the Kruise Flow execution-week snapshot (week starting 2026-08-24). All retrieved documents are listed in the Appendix.\\n\\nTop-level summary (what changed since previous brief)\\n- Kruise Flow — RBAC: Completed (status → Done). Evidence: admin full-access permission matrix implemented and session permission loading from IAM reported complete on 2026-08-26. (Source: KRUISE WORKFLOW OFFICIAL — daily 26-Aug-2026; see Exec snapshot entry \\\"kruise-workflow-rbac-implementation\\\", Update 2026-08-26.)\\n- Kruise COS — Planner / Task Module: End-to-end Planner → Gaps & Risks → User Review → Re-plan → Task flow validated and finalized on 2026-08-26, but the Planner-Agent implementation row still lists 90% and “final fixes/testing pending” in the execution snapshot (overlap/discrepancy noted). (Sources: KRUISE WORKFLOW OFFICIAL — daily 26-Aug-2026; execution-week snapshot — entries \\\"kruise-cos-end-to-end-integration-validation\\\" and \\\"kruise-cos-planner-agent-implementation\\\", as_of 2026-08-26.)\\n- Kruise Flow — Dynamic Rack Recommendation (Inventory): Phase 1 complete (Inventory Management API integration + initial rack-recommendation) — milestone now ~50%; Dynamic Agent implementation remains outstanding (delayed/backlog pick-up). (Source: KRUISE WORKFLOW OFFICIAL — daily 26-Aug-2026; execution snapshot \\\"kruise-workflow-stock-in-stock-out-enhancements\\\", update 2026-08-26.)\\n- Kruise Flow — Test Suite UI/UX: Completed on 2026-08-26 (moved to 100%). (Source: KRUISE WORKFLOW OFFICIAL — daily 26-Aug-2026; execution snapshot \\\"kruise-workflow-test-suite-ui-ux\\\", update 2026-08-26.)\\n- Kruise COS — RAG architecture & RAG backend node: Deferred on 2026-08-26 (0% started; priority shifted to Inventory/Dynamic Agent work). This is a material scope/priority change. (Source: KRUISE WORKFLOW OFFICIAL — daily 26-Aug-2026; execution snapshot \\\"kruise-cos-architecture-refinement\\\" and \\\"kruise-cos-rag-backend-node-definition\\\", update 2026-08-26.)\\n- Kruise CRM & Stock & Inspecto — discrete completions recorded today (26-Aug): CRM custom notifications and MongoDB→Postgres migration analysis completed; StockOps PRF backend changes and workflow history items deployed/tested; Inspecto token-anomaly detector and RBAC UI/tasks show completed work. These are reported completions but prior-day status not always present for direct day-to-day diffs (see Appendix). (Sources: Kruise CRM daily 26-Aug-2026; Stock_Management_official daily 26-Aug-2026; 7.INSPECTO daily 26-Aug-2026.)\\n\\nWhat needs your attention (prioritized; 3–5 items)\\n1) Confirm Planner-Agent final fixes & QA sign-off (IMMEDIATE — action within 24 hours)\\n- Short description: Execution snapshot shows Planner→Gaps & Risks→User Review→Re-plan→Task flow reported finalized on 26-Aug (end-to-end validation), but Planner-Agent milestone still lists 90% with explicit risk notes (final fixes / end-to-end testing pending). There is a reported overlap/discrepancy that could hide remaining critical defects.\\n- Impact / severity: High — may block Task Module automation, demos, or any releases depending on tasks being auto-created.\\n- Affected milestones: kruise-cos-planner-agent-implementation; kruise-cos-end-to-end-integration-validation; kruise-cos-plan-to-task-workflow.\\n- Current owner(s): Shrish (resource_name on Planner/End-to-end entries in reports/snapshot).\\n- Proposed next actions for you: (a) Ask Shrish + QA to confirm a single canonical status (Are there failing test cases? Is there a release-blocking bug?) and surface any open high/critical defects; (b) require QA sign-off artifact (CI test pass + list of open defects with severity) posted to the Kruise release tracker; (c) if tests are failing, authorize one-day bug-fix priority to reach green.\\n- Deadline / SLA: 24 hours (to avoid release scheduling risk for week-ending deliveries).\\n- Confidence: Medium→High. Evidence: execution-week snapshot entries \\\"kruise-cos-planner-agent-implementation\\\" (90%/risk) and \\\"kruise-cos-end-to-end-integration-validation\\\" (100%/extended by 1 day) — see Appendix links.\\n\\n2) Decide whether to re-prioritize/resume RAG architecture work (near-term decision requested)\\n- Short description: RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) architecture study (node definition, Qdrant integration, FE/BE contract) was deferred on 26-Aug in favor of Inventory/Dynamic Agent work.\\n- Impact / severity: High — RAG is foundational for retrieval/augmentation features; deferred architecture increases risk of integration/feature instability for COS features that rely on knowledge retrieval.\\n- Affected milestones: kruise-cos-architecture-refinement; kruise-cos-rag-requirement-amp-architecture; kruise-cos-rag-backend-node-definition.\\n- Current owner(s): Shrish (resource_name on deferred RAG entries).\\n- Proposed next actions for you: (a) Approve the deferral formally OR (b) reallocate a small cross-functional squad (1 architect + 1 backend) to start the minimal FE/BE contract and retrieval PoC this week, or (c) schedule a 30–60 minute decision meeting with Shrish + Architect + Product to decide scope. Recommend (b) if retrieval-dependent demos/releases are scheduled.\\n- Deadline / SLA: Decision within 48 hours recommended; escalate within 72 hours if no decision.\\n- Confidence: High (explicit “deferred” status in the daily 26-Aug report + snapshot).\\n\\n3) Complete Dynamic Rack Recommendation (Stock-In/Out) to enable E2E warehouse validation\\n- Short description: Phase 1 (Inventory API integration + initial rack recommendation) is complete (~50%); Dynamic Agent implementation is outstanding and was pulled from backlog (delaying E2E).\\n- Impact / severity: Medium — incomplete rack/putaway automation will prevent full Stock-In/Stock-Out E2E validation and may require manual interventions during release.\\n- Affected milestones: kruise-workflow-stock-in-stock-out-enhancements; Kruise ERP change-request support interfaces.\\n- Current owner(s): Shrish (reported on Dynamic Rack entry); Nexus with Stock team (Prasanna reported StockOps Dev changes same day).\\n- Proposed next actions for you: (a) Authorize a focused development day for Dynamic Agent completion and QA; (b) require explicit go/no-go criteria for Stock E2E (list of happy-path scenarios + manual fallbacks) be published to the Stock tracker.\\n- Deadline / SLA: Recommend completion or blockage report within 72 hours to keep weekly E2E validation window.\\n- Confidence: High (execution snapshot shows Phase 1 completed and remaining work clearly identified).\\n\\n4) Resolve plotting/data-ingestion time-conflict (affects CEO analytics/visualization)\\n- Short description: Sandboxed code execution & plotting integration progress shows delays and inconsistent percent-completion; teams reported a data-ingestion time-conflict and IAM-priority shift blocked implementation.\\n- Impact / severity: Medium — will affect Athena’s in-chat plotting/CEO analytics user experience if not resolved.\\n- Affected milestones: kruise-cos-sandboxed-code-execution-plotting; kruise-cos-ceo-analytics-visualization.\\n- Current owner(s): Jairam / Pavan (per daily updates showing work and troubleshooting).\\n- Proposed next actions for you: (a) Ask DevOps + Jairam/Pavan for a short bug-intake and triage meeting (30–60 min) to assign ownership and ETA; (b) consider short-term scope reduction (return static graphs) if resolution will exceed 72 hours.\\n- Deadline / SLA: Request triage within 48 hours; if unresolved, require escalation or scope reduction decision within 72 hours.\\n- Confidence: Medium (reported data-ingestion time-conflict and priority shift in execution snapshot/daily updates).\\n\\n5) Freeze feature documentation gaps for mobile/production APIs (prevent downstream rework)\\n- Short description: Transaction-level Production API mapping to mobile screens is ~70% complet…(+11173 chars)\",",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":-800,
			"width":980,
			"height":460
		},
